/**
 * @page name_concept TName concept
 *
 * @brief Strongly typed object naming concept.
 *
 * TName is a strong type used to represent object identifiers
 * in a safe and explicit way.
 *
 * Instead of using raw strings, TName encodes the object
 * domain in its template parameter.
 *
 * This prevents accidental comparison or assignment of
 * names belonging to different object types.
 *
 * Example:
 * @code
 * struct Service {};
 * struct Device {};
 *
 * using ServiceName = TName<Service>;
 * using DeviceName  = TName<Device>;
 *
 * ServiceName s{ "Audio" };
 * DeviceName  d{ "Audio" };
 *
 * // s == d; // compilation error
 * @endcode
 *
 * Invalid state:
 * Each TName has a well-defined invalid value provided
 * via TNameTraits.
 *
 * This allows explicit representation of uninitialized
 * or invalid names.
 *
 * Performance:
 * TName precomputes its hash value on construction.
 * This enables efficient usage in unordered containers
 * and real-time systems.
 *
 * Related API:
 * - @ref TName
 * - @ref TNameTraits
 * - @ref NameValue
 */
